winebus: the motors ride the game's own packet instead of costing the link one.

WHAT WAS WRONG, measured twice from the same two traces by analysts told to
refute each other. The pad's Bluetooth output pipe drains about 65 reports a
second. A title that rumbles through XInput STILL writes the pad's own 0x31 once
a frame: 16,995 of Beast's 18,149 in one session, every valid flag zero, both
motors zero -- a packet that tells the pad to do nothing, sixty times a second.
That leaves roughly five slots a second for anybody else. mgvf-0010's thread
offered thirty. A shallow queue filled within a handful of our writes, and from
then on EVERY writer paid about 21 ms a packet -- the game's own synchronous
write included, on a thread running at frame cadence, holding the device lock
on the one thread wine dispatches every IRP through.

The dose-response is in the trace: with 0, 8, 16, 24 and 32 of our writes a
second, the share of the game's own writes taking over 10 ms was 3.9%, 16%,
41%, 66% and 95%, and the marginal cost per packet of ours stayed at 25-30 ms
across every band. The queue drains over ~200 ms after our last write. That is
a queue and not a lock. And the positive control is in the NATIVE title's own
trace: in the 1.44% of moments Mortal Shell's own rate exceeds 64 a second, it
suffers 82.8% of every slow write it ever makes, with nothing of ours involved.

WHAT WAS NOT WRONG, and the day was spent proving it: CPU (bluetoothd 1.8% to
2.9% of a core), the pad's input stream, a control-channel handshake, Bluetooth
audio, sniff mode, Wi-Fi coexistence, which thread makes the write, its QoS,
the device lock, wineserver round trips, the packet's content, its sequence
tag. Each is refuted with a number in the notes that accompany this series.
The first six were mine, and each died because the experiment that killed it
moved two variables and concluded about one.

WHY SONY DOES NOT PAY. Its library carries the motors INSIDE the heartbeat: 283
of Mortal Shell's 8,608 packets have byte 5 set, and rumble costs it zero
additional packets. So the packet has to be free -- not rare, free -- and the
game's inert one already is.

WHAT THIS DOES. With XInputRumbleRide set, every client 0x31 passes through a
copy on its way out, as it already did for mgvf-0009. If the packet asks the
pad for nothing, the wanted motor pair is stamped into it: the two bits the
legacy motors need, the two motor bytes, and a CRC over the result. The
haptics thread notes that the client is writing and stays silent; it writes a
packet of its own only after a hundred milliseconds without one -- a title that
stopped, or one that never wrote and owns the whole budget. The stop rides the
same way, because the thread that used to carry it is the one now silent. A
packet with any flag set is the game driving lights, triggers or its own
motors and is never touched.

The deadband of mgvf-0018 moves into the extension so that both writers consult
one record of what the pad was last given, and mgvf-0016's gain is applied
after the stamp by the same function that applies it to the thread's packets,
so the two writers cannot drift apart on either.

THREE THINGS A REVIEW CAUGHT BEFORE THIS SHIPPED, kept here because each is a
stuck motor. The thread's private "last value I sent" was blind to what the
ride had sent, so a stop asked while the client was silent could compare equal
to a stale record and be dropped -- the pad buzzing through a loading screen;
the record is shared now and the pair the pad already has is never worth a
packet, whichever writer gave it. The client's tick was stamped before the
inert test, so a game writing a flagged packet every frame silenced the thread
for ever; only an inert packet silences it now, and such a game is served the
old way at the old cost. And the record was noted after the write, so the two
writers could cross and leave the record behind the pad -- and claiming it
before the write did not close the mirror ordering, where the ride notes first
and its packet lands last. So the overlap is forbidden outright: while the
thread is on the wire the ride does not stamp, and if the client reappeared
during that write the thread judges its value again at the gate.

OFF BY DEFAULT, because it has not been felt yet. What has been measured is the
mechanism and the arithmetic; whether a stamped heartbeat feels like the
thread's packets did is for a hand on the pad. The reader in diagnostics/
counts "rode the client's 0x31" against "telling the motors" so the trace says
which writer carried what.

WHAT IS NOT COVERED. A pad mgvf-0005 presents as wired has its client's 0x02
translated in dualsense_usb_set_output_report, and the ride does not reach into
that route: the thread's own packet passes through the same function and the
two are not told apart there. The silence window is a constant, not measured
against any title's cadence beyond one at sixty a frame. And the frame cost was
never read off a frame counter -- the game's own 60/s stream stood in for it,
and it is that stream this removes the pressure from.

Signed-off-by: MacGameVideoFix
